WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT SAY
==============================================================================================
  This is a LOWER BOUND on both sides of the question:
    * a synonym absent from BOTH production tables is invisible here, so the
      wired count can only be understated;
    * F-167's 90/374 'present in the payload' is likewise a lower bound, biased
      down by the same blindness -- it did not count ATP on PMC12096016/strict.

  It does NOT licence a matcher change. The auditor ruled the matcher's
  substring rule and its match-against-ADMITTED-PROCESSES design are both
  correct (D-088 clause 6; F-167 trap 3), and located the defect UPSTREAM in
  canonicalisation. This probe sizes the problem and proposes nothing.

